  "info": {
    "title": "Factory plain domain types",
    "version": "0.2.0",
    "description": "AGENT CHANGE POLICY: Never change anything in this file without first consulting the user and obtaining explicit approval for the proposed changes. This includes additions, removals, renames, constraints, annotations, formatting and automated rewrites. Do not infer approval from a broader implementation task. Before proposing or editing domain fields, read the storage types in crates/factory-types/record.proto and the ownership rules in crates/factory-types/fslayout.json. Check whether the requested functionality already belongs to RecordEnvelope, RecordDependencies, LifecycleIndex, PendingTransaction or FileChange. Do not duplicate storage identity, common metadata, dependencies, lifecycle timestamps, allocation counters, transaction recovery or path-derived ownership in domain payloads. Add a domain field only for distinct domain meaning with a concrete consumer; explain that distinction when requesting approval. Existing work-tracking slug IDs are not a template for adding redundant IDs to new domain types. Numeric Factory identity remains in the record envelope. Agent persona and skills belong to DomainAgent and supply derived construction dependencies; work-tracking relationships are not automatically construction prerequisites. This replaces the unshipped Type Safety experiment, not the legacy application's schema."
  },
